cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Prediction instability audits for fitted models"
version: 3.1.1
date-released: 2026-09-19
url: "https://github.com/finite-sample/stable-cart"
repository-code: "https://github.com/finite-sample/stable-cart"
authors:
  - family-names: "Sood"
    given-names: "Gaurav"
  - family-names: "Bhosle"
    given-names: "Arav"
abstract: >-
  A Python package for auditing how predictions change when a complete
  model-building procedure is refitted on bootstrap samples. It preserves
  individual prediction distributions, implements label-invariant and
  probability-vector metrics for classification, reports Monte Carlo error,
  and constructs validation-score versus instability frontiers.
keywords:
  - machine learning
  - stability
  - sklearn
  - prediction stability
  - bootstrap
  - model validation
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
